@startuml Entity Lifecycle
title Entity Lifecycle & NPC Conversion System

state "Non-Existent" as None

state "Enemy Agent" as Enemy {
    state "Spawned" as ESpawn
    state "Active" as EActive
    state "Defeated" as EDefeat
    state "Surrendered" as ESurr

    ESpawn --> EActive : combat begins
    EActive --> EDefeat : HP ≤ 0
    EActive --> ESurr : morale break
    EActive --> EActive : takes turns
}

state "NPC Agent" as NPC {
    state "Spawned" as NSpawn
    state "Active" as NActive
    state "Prisoner" as NPrisoner
    state "Ally" as NAlly
    state "Hostile" as NHostile
    state "Vendor" as NVendor

    NSpawn --> NActive : introduced
    NSpawn --> NVendor : is_vendor=True
    NActive --> NPrisoner : subdued
    NActive --> NAlly : befriended
    NActive --> NHostile : betrayal
    NActive --> NActive : takes turns (opportunistic)
    NVendor --> NVendor : accepts purchases\ncan_act=False (static)
    NVendor --> NActive : can_act=True (dynamic)
}

' Creation paths
None --> Enemy : DM spawns via\nRoundSynthesis.enemy_spawns
None --> NPC : DM spawns via\nRoundSynthesis.npc_spawns

' Conversion paths (CRITICAL: agent_id preserved!)
Enemy --> NPC : deescalate_enemy_to_npc()\nvia Deescalation schema
NPC --> Enemy : escalate_npc_to_enemy()\nvia Escalation schema

' Specific conversion triggers
EActive --> NPrisoner : subdue_enemy_to_prisoner()\n(non-lethal defeat)
ESurr --> NPrisoner : deescalation with\ndisposition="prisoner"
EActive --> NAlly : deescalation with\ndisposition="ally"

NHostile --> EActive : escalation with\ntemplate="desperate_fighter"
NActive --> EActive : attacked by players

note right of Enemy
    Full combat capabilities:
    - Tactical AI (personality-based)
    - Attack/defend/tactical actions
    - Target prioritization
    - Morale tracking

    LLM prompts: ~2000 tokens
    Action set: attack, defend, tactical,
                special abilities

    agent_id: STABLE across conversions
    Example: "ene_a1b2c3d4"
end note

note right of NPC
    Limited capabilities:
    - Simple LLM client (~500 tokens)
    - No tactical AI
    - No attack actions
    - Opportunistic acting (pass when boring)

    Action set: flee, hide, plead, comply,
                dialogue, assist, pass

    Vendor capabilities (optional):
    - is_vendor=True flag
    - vendor_inventory (List[VendorItem])
    - vendor_type (human_trader, vending_machine, etc.)
    - accepts_purchases flag
    - can_act=False for static vendors (no LLM)

    agent_id: STABLE across conversions
    Example: "npc_a1b2c3d4" OR "ene_a1b2c3d4"
              (preserves enemy ID if converted)
end note

note bottom of None
    Conversion mechanics:
    - agent_id NEVER changes
    - Health/void/wounds preserved
    - Disposition tracked (prisoner/ally/hostile)
    - NO keyword detection - all via Pydantic schemas
end note

state "Conversion Process" as Conv {
    state "DM declares in RoundSynthesis" as DMDeclare
    state "Coordinator processes" as CoordProc
    state "State updated" as StateUpd

    DMDeclare --> CoordProc : deescalations/escalations/npc_spawns
    CoordProc --> StateUpd : agent_conversion.py functions
}

Enemy ..> Conv : triggers
NPC ..> Conv : triggers

note left of Conv
    Conversion schemas:

    NPCSpawn:
    - agent_id (new)
    - name, description
    - disposition
    - is_vendor (optional)
    - vendor_inventory (optional)
    - vendor_type (optional)
    - accepts_purchases (optional)

    Deescalation:
    - agent_id (existing enemy)
    - reason
    - disposition
    - outcome_description

    Escalation:
    - agent_id (existing NPC)
    - reason
    - enemy_template
    - outcome_description
end note

@enduml
